y interpolated without URL encoding. An attacker could inject additional query parameters.\n\n**Architecture Strengths:**\n- ✅ CSRF protection properly implemented with tokens + SameSite=Strict cookies\n- ✅ No hardcoded secrets or API keys\n- ✅ Uses `credentials: \"include\"` for session-based auth\n- ✅ Socket.IO auth callback pattern ensures fresh tokens on reconnect\n\n**Watch:** React-markdown dependency could enable XSS if user content is rendered unsanitized. Verify usage in components not shown here.\n\nThe overall security posture is **moderate-to-good** for frontend code, but backend validation is critical for all of these measures to be effective. Risk score reflects the query injection issue + potential markdown XSS exposure.\n",
